cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  What a DNA language model knows about real eDNA reads: off-targets,
  novelty and chimeras (Evo 2, version 2)
message: If you use these results or scripts, please cite them as below.
type: software
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
authors:
  - given-names: Maia
    family-names: Kaplan
    affiliation: Universidad de Buenos Aires / IQUIBICEN
repository-code: 'https://github.com/maiakaplan03/evo2-edna-real-reads'
abstract: >-
  Tests whether the Evo 2 (7B) genomic foundation model stores the
  information that traditional eDNA pipeline steps use - COI filters,
  database identity, chimera detection - by scoring 200,898 real COI
  metabarcoding sequences (Brazilian soil, abyssal sediment) and simulated
  contamination cohorts in one shared space. Covers off-target reads that
  pass every COI check, an identity-stratified novelty ladder, and
  reference-free localisation of chimera junctions. Version 1 (simulated
  data only) is at github.com/maiakaplan03/evo2-edna-novelty-v1.
keywords:
  - environmental DNA
  - metabarcoding
  - genomic language model
  - Evo 2
  - embeddings
  - off-target amplicons
  - chimera detection
  - novelty detection
license: MIT
